From 4d1018ae554e2994d7682878e49fb88fca2244d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "H. Peter Anvin" <hpa@zytor.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Nov 2025 21:37:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Fix baud rate settings

Fix numerous settings with the baud rate setting code.

- It is not valid to assume the baud rate is part of c_cflag.
  Among other things, this breaks on Hurd, many BSDs, and Linux
  with glibc 2.42+.
- Don't use TIOCSSERIAL on Linux. It breaks other applications which
  expect to have the serial port set to 38400.  Use cfsetobaud() if
  it exists (glibc 2.42+) otherwise the termios2 interface (TCSETS2).
- <linux/termios.h> and <termios.h> are mutually exclusive.
- Prove a mechanism for probing new Bxxx constants if necessary.
- For platforms where speed_t is "sane", use it directly.
- Some platforms need _GNU_SOURCE and/or _XOPEN_SOURCE for all
  <termios.h> features to be enabled.

Signed-off-by: H. Peter Anvin <hpa@zytor.com>
